{"step_index":189,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:37:03Z","thinking":"**Re-evaluating the problem's scope**\n\nThe goal is to prove `prove_2a2555cc`. A key question arises: is a full re-proof of graph theory required? It seems like this isn't necessary. The focus must remain on the theorem itself.\n```lean\ntheorem prove_2a2555cc : Candidate := by\n  intro V _ _\n```\n\n\n**Analyzing graph invariants' definitions**\n\nThe definitions of radius and total domination number are being inspected for potential relationships. Examining `minUpTo` in the eccentricity definition is key. The question becomes whether it is possible to relate a vertex's eccentricity to the total domination number. Choosing a vertex that minimizes eccentricity allows relating it directly to the radius. The goal simplifies to proving this minimized eccentricity is less than or equal to the total domination number.\n\n\n**Attempting proof by contradiction**\n\nAssume total domination number is less than the radius, which implies, for every vertex, there exists another vertex further away than the total domination number. This would contradict the existence of a total dominating set, as every vertex must be within distance 1 of a member of the set. The triangle inequality can be applied since $S$ is a dominating set.\n\n**Examining relationships between vertices**\n\nIf `dist(u,w) > k` for all `u, w`, it means for a set `S` of size `k`, every vertex in the graph must be at a distance greater than `k` from every other vertex.  However, vertices are distance 1 from some member in the dominating set `S`. Therefore `dist(u,w)` must be less than or equal to `dist(s_i, s_j) + 2`, which is a contradiction if `dist(u,w) > k`.\n\n\n**Evaluating a counterexample graph**\n\nA specific example, P6, is now tested to gain intuition about the relationship between a dominating set and vertex eccentricity. Observing the distances between vertices in a dominating set and the eccentricities in the graph helps to understand the implications of the domination number. The minimum eccentricity is analyzed and compared to the cardinality of the chosen dominating set.\n\n**Generalizing the eccentricity observation**\n\nFocusing on the behavior of a vertex minimizing the maximum distance to the dominating set, a bound on this maximum distance is derived: `D(x*) <= |S| - 1`. Because every vertex is distance 1 from some member of the dominating set, the distance from `x*` to any vertex `y` is at most |S|. This implies the eccentricity of the vertex minimizing the maximum distance to the dominating set is bounded by the size of the dominating set.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"search_web","args":{"query":"\"radius\" \"total domination\" graph","toolAction":"Searching the web","toolSummary":"Search radius total domination"}}]}
{"step_index":191,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:37:16Z","thinking":"**Re-examining Challenge_2a2555cc**\n\nInvestigating the possibility of proving `Candidate` within Lean 4. Reviewing existing Lean 4 proofs, specifically `scratch.lean`, to identify potentially relevant lemmas. Identified and recalled existing proven lemmas: `finset_min_getD_le`, `radius_le_eccentricity`, and `finset_min_getD`.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":false,"Description":"Add ballWithin lemmas to scratch.lean","EndLine":41,"Instruction":"Add ballWithin lemmas to scratch.lean","ReplacementContent":"import Mathlib\nimport LeanProject.GraphInvariantsComputable\n\nopen SimpleGraph\n\nlemma ballWithin_zero {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V] (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (v : V) :\n    GraphCalc.ballWithin G 0 v = {v} := rfl\n\nlemma ballWithin_subset_succ {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V] (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (k : ℕ) (v : V) :\n    GraphCalc.ballWithin G k v ⊆ GraphCalc.ballWithin G (k + 1) v := by\n  dsimp [GraphCalc.ballWithin]\n  exact Finset.subset_union_left\n\nlemma mem_ballWithin_succ_of_adj {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V] (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\n    (k : ℕ) (v u w : V) (hu : u ∈ GraphCalc.ballWithin G k v) (hadj : G.Adj u w) :\n    w ∈ GraphCalc.ballWithin G (k + 1) v := by\n  dsimp [GraphCalc.ballWithin]\n  apply Finset.mem_union_right\n  apply Finset.mem_biUnion.mpr\n  refine ⟨u, hu, ?_⟩\n  rw [Finset.mem_filter]\n  exact ⟨Finset.mem_univ w, hadj⟩\n\nlemma mem_ballWithin_of_walk_reverse {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V] (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\n    {v w : V} (q : G.Walk w v) : w ∈ GraphCalc.ballWithin G q.length v := by\n  induction q with\n  | nil =>\n    dsimp [GraphCalc.ballWithin]\n    exact Finset.mem_singleton_self _\n  | cons hadj _ ih =>\n    rw [SimpleGraph.Walk.length_cons]\n    exact mem_ballWithin_succ_of_adj G _ _ _ _ ih hadj.symm\n\nlemma mem_ballWithin_of_walk {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V] (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\n    {v w : V} (p : G.Walk v w) : w ∈ GraphCalc.ballWithin G p.length v := by\n  have h := mem_ballWithin_of_walk_reverse G p.reverse\n  rw [SimpleGraph.Walk.length_reverse] at h\n  exact h\n\nlemma finset_min_getD_le {s : Finset ℕ} {b : ℕ} (hb : b ∈ s) :\n    s.min.getD 0 ≤ b := by\n  have h : s.min ≤ WithTop.some b := Finset.inf_le hb\n  cases hm : s.min with\n  | top =>\n    rw [hm] at h\n    simp at h\n  | coe m =>\n    rw [hm] at h\n    exact WithTop.coe_le_coe.mp h\n\nlemma radius_le_eccentricity {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (v : V) :\n    GraphCalc.radius G ≤ GraphCalc.eccentricity G v := by\n  apply finset_min_getD_le\n  apply Finset.mem_image.mpr\n  exact ⟨v, Finset.mem_univ v, rfl⟩\n\nlemma finset_min_getD_le_of_mem (n : ℕ) {s : Finset ℕ} {b : ℕ} (hb : b ∈ s) :\n    s.min.getD n ≤ b := by\n  have h : s.min ≤ WithTop.some b := Finset.inf_le hb\n  cases hm : s.min with\n  | top =>\n    rw [hm] at h\n    simp at h\n  | coe m =>\n    rw [hm] at h\n    exact WithTop.coe_le_coe.mp h\n\nlemma eccentricity_le_of_ballWithin_eq_univ {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (v : V) (k : ℕ)\n    (hkle : k ≤ Fintype.card V) (heq : GraphCalc.ballWithin G k v = Finset.univ) :\n    GraphCalc.eccentricity G v ≤ k := by\n  dsimp [GraphCalc.eccentricity, GraphCalc.minUpTo]\n  apply finset_min_getD_le_of_mem (Fintype.card V)\n  rw [Finset.mem_filter, Finset.mem_range]\n  exact ⟨Nat.lt_succ_of_le hkle, heq⟩\n\nlemma ballWithin_univ_of_subset {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (v : V) (k : ℕ) (S : Finset V)\n    (hdom : GraphCalc.IsTotalDominatingSet G S)\n    (hsub : S ⊆ GraphCalc.ballWithin G k v) :\n    GraphCalc.ballWithin G (k + 1) v = Finset.univ := by\n  apply Finset.eq_univ_of_forall\n  intro u\n  obtain ⟨s, hs, hadj⟩ := hdom u\n  have hsb : s ∈ GraphCalc.ballWithin G k v := hsub hs\n  exact mem_ballWithin_succ_of_adj G k v s u hsb hadj.symm","StartLine":1,"TargetContent":"import Mathlib\nimport LeanProject.GraphInvariantsComputable\n\nlemma finset_min_getD_le {s : Finset ℕ} {b : ℕ} (hb : b ∈ s) :\n    s.min.getD 0 ≤ b := by\n  have h : s.min ≤ WithTop.some b := Finset.inf_le hb\n  cases hm : s.min with\n  | top =>\n    rw [hm] at h\n    simp at h\n  | coe m =>\n    rw [hm] at h\n    exact WithTop.coe_le_coe.mp h\n\nlemma radius_le_eccentricity {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (v : V) :\n    GraphCalc.radius G ≤ GraphCalc.eccentricity G v := by\n  apply finset_min_getD_le\n  apply Finset.mem_image.mpr\n  exact ⟨v, Finset.mem_univ v, rfl⟩\n\nlemma finset_min_getD_le_of_mem (n : ℕ) {s : Finset ℕ} {b : ℕ} (hb : b ∈ s) :\n    s.min.getD n ≤ b := by\n  have h : s.min ≤ WithTop.some b := Finset.inf_le hb\n  cases hm : s.min with\n  | top =>\n    rw [hm] at h\n    simp at h\n  | coe m =>\n    rw [hm] at h\n    exact WithTop.coe_le_coe.mp h\n\nlemma eccentricity_le_of_ballWithin_eq_univ {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (v : V) (k : ℕ)\n    (hkle : k ≤ Fintype.card V) (heq : GraphCalc.ballWithin G k v = Finset.univ) :\n    GraphCalc.eccentricity G v ≤ k := by\n  dsimp [GraphCalc.eccentricity, GraphCalc.minUpTo]\n  apply finset_min_getD_le_of_mem (Fintype.card V)\n  rw [Finset.mem_filter, Finset.mem_range]\n  exact ⟨Nat.lt_succ_of_le hkle, heq⟩","TargetFile":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_2a2555cc/scratch.lean","toolAction":"Editing file","toolSummary":"Update scratch.lean with ballWithin lemmas"}}]}
