 connected subgraph. -/\n105: def IsConnectedZeroForcingSet (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (S : Finset V) : Prop :=\n106:   G.IsZeroForcingSet S ∧ (G.induce (↑S)).Connected\n107: \n108: /-- Connected zero forcing number `Z_c(G)`. -/\n109: noncomputable def connectedZeroForcingNumber (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ :=\n110:   sInf { k | ∃ S : Finset V, S.card = k ∧ G.IsConnectedZeroForcingSet S }\n111: \n112: /-- `s` totally dominates `G`: every vertex has a neighbour in `s` (a vertex\n113: does not dominate itself). -/\n114: def IsTotalDominatingSet (G : SimpleGraph V) (s : Finset V) : Prop :=\n115:   ∀ v : V, ∃ w ∈ s, G.Adj v w\n116: \n117: /-- Total domination number `γ_t(G)`. Undefined (here: `sInf ∅ = 0`) on a graph\n118: with an isolated vertex; the computable mirror carries an explicit definedness\n119: predicate, and the exporters emit it as a hypothesis. -/\n120: noncomputable def totalDominationNumber (G : SimpleGraph V) : ℕ :=\n121:   sInf { n | ∃ s : Finset V, s.card = n ∧ G.IsTotalDominatingSet s }\n122: \n123: /-- `s` is an edge cover: every vertex lies on some edge of `s`. -/\n124: def IsEdgeCoverFinset (G : SimpleGraph V) (s : Finset (Sym2 V)) : Prop :=\n125:   ↑s ⊆ G.edgeSet ∧ ∀ v : V, ∃ e ∈ s, v ∈ e\n126: \n127: /-- Edge cover number `ρ(G)`: minimum size of an edge cover. Undefined on a\n128: graph with an isolated vertex. -/\n129: noncomputable def edgeCoverNumber (G : SimpleGraph V) : ℕ :=\n130:   sInf { n | ∃ s : Finset (Sym2 V), s.card = n ∧ G.IsEdgeCoverFinset s }\n131: \n132: /-- Sub-total domination number: least `t` whose `t` largest degrees sum to at\n133: least `n` (Davila). -/\n134: noncomputable def subTotalDominationNumber (G : SimpleGraph V)\n135:     [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ :=\n136:   sInf { t | Fintype.card V ≤ ((G.degreesDesc).take t).sum }\n137: \n138: /-- `f` is a Roman dominating function: every vertex labelled `0` has a\n139: neighbour labelled `2`. -/\n140: def IsRomanDominatingFunction (G : SimpleGraph V) (f : V → Fin 3) : Prop :=\n141:   ∀ v : V, f v = 0 → ∃ u : V, G.Adj v u ∧ f u = 2\n142: \n143: /-- Roman domination number `γ_R(G)`: minimum weight `Σ f v` over Roman\n144: dominating functions. -/\n145: noncomputable def romanDominationNumber (G : SimpleGraph V) : ℕ :=\n146:   sInf { n | ∃ f : V → Fin 3, G.IsRomanDominatingFunction f ∧ ∑ v, (f v : ℕ) = n }\n147: \n148: /-- `f` is a double Roman dominating function: a vertex labelled `0` has a\n149: neighbour labelled `3` or two neighbours labelled `2`, and a vertex labelled `1`\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
